    "evidence_text": "Methodology ::: Overall Task\tOur task is the following, where $t$ denotes \u201ctarget\": Given a target character $c_t$ with HLA set $H_t$, recover the language style of $c_t$ without any dialogue of $c_t$ provided.\n\nIt is a character specific language model refined from a general language model.\n\nMethodology ::: Character Space Module (CSM)\tCSM learns how to rank characters.\n\ndataset, and $P_{u,i} = 0$ otherwise.\n\nThis is analogous to factoring the matrix $P$ into two separate matrices, where one contains the latent factors for characters, and the other contains the latent factors for HLAs.\n\nMethodology ::: Character Community Module (CCM)\tCCM aims to divide characters (other than $c_t$) into a positive community and a negative set.\n\nThis allows us to map our character space into two-dimensions, where similar characters from our embedding space have higher probability of being mapped close by.\n\nEvaluation ::: Automatic Evaluation Setup ::: Five Evaluation Characters\tare chosen, one from each of the five testing\n\nEach is a well-known character from a separate TV show, and acts as a target character $c_t$ for evaluation of every model.",
